ward force** is  \n\n\\[\nF = m\\,(g+a)\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 1. Total lifting force  \n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\ng+a &= 9.81 + 1.5 = 11.31\\;\\text{m\u202fs}^{-2}\\\\[2mm]\nF &= 1200\\;\\text{kg}\\times 11.31\\;\\text{m\u202fs}^{-2}= \\boxed{1.3572\\times10^{4}\\ \\text{N}}\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 2. Torque on the winch shaft  \n\nAssuming the force acts perpendicular to the shaft ( \\(\\theta = 90^{\\circ}\\) ),  \n\n\\[\n\\tau = r\\,F = 0.08\\;\\text{m}\\times 1.3572\\times10^{4}\\;\\text{N}\n      = \\boxed{1.09\\times10^{3}\\ \\text{N·m}}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 3. Work done to raise the load 15\u202fm  \n\nThe work is the force multiplied by the displacement (force parallel to motion):\n\n\\[\nW = F\\,d = 1.3572\\times10^{4}\\;\\text{N}\\times 15\\;\\text{m}\n    = \\boxed{2.04\\times10^{5}\\ \\text{J}}\n\\]\n\n(Equivalently, \\(W = m g d + \\tfrac12 m v^{2}\\) gives 2.04\u202f×\u202f10⁵\u202fJ, the same result.)\n\n---\n\n### 4. Mechanical power required  \n\n\\[\nP = \\frac{W}{t}= \\frac{2.04\\times10^{5}\\ \\text{J}}{4.5\\ \\text{s}}\n   = \\boxed{4.52\\times10^{4}\\ \\text{W}} \\; (\\approx 45.2\\ \\text{kW})\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 5. Tensile stress in the shaft  \n\nCross‑sectional area of the solid shaft  \n\n\\[\nA = \\pi r^{2}= \\pi (0.08\\ \\text{m})^{2}\n   = \\pi(0.0064)\\ \\text{m}^{2}\n   = 2.0106\\times10^{-2}\\ \\text{m}^{2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\sigma = \\frac{F}{A}\n        = \\frac{1.3572\\times10^{4}\\ \\text{N}}{2.0106\\times10^{-2}\\ \\text{m}^{2}}\n        = \\boxed{6.75\\times10^{5}\\ \\text{Pa}} \n        \\; (\\approx 0.675\\ \\text{MPa})\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 6. Axial strain in the shaft  \n\n\\[\n\\epsilon = \\frac{\\sigma}{E}\n          = \\frac{6.75\\times10^{5}\\ \\text{Pa}}{210\\times10^{9}\\ \\text{Pa}}\n          = \\boxed{3.2\\times10^{-6}}\n\\]\n\n(≈\u202f3.2\u202fµε, i.e., 3.2\u202fµstrain.)\n\n---\n\n**Summary of results**\n\n| Quantity | Symbol | Value | Units |\n|----------|--------|-------|-------|\n| Lifting force | \\(F\\) | \\(1.